      "Reykjavík is the capital of Iceland, and the northernmost capital of a sovereign state in the world, with a municipal population of about 140,000 at the start of 2026 and, together with the rest of the Capital Region, about 63 per cent of the country. The name means 'smoky bay' in Old Norse — the first settlers saw geothermal steam. The city is small and low-rise, heated by geothermal water, with almost no industrial chimneys.",
